  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobile Care Project to provide primary healthcare services for NCDs and MHPSS support through individual psychological consultations and group sessions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve efficiency and resource allocation, the project will adopt a new service delivery model that better integrates with local healthcare providers.The key principle is to differentiate responsibilities between local family doctors and the mobile teams, ensuring that specialists focus on cases with genuine medical needs.Service Delivery Structure:1. Settlements with Family Doctors&#x2022;Local doctors will conduct initial assessments and refer patients to our specialists only when necessary.&#x2022;Our mobile team will include a family doctor, psychologist, and nurse.&#x2022;When 20 patients are referred to a specialist, they will join the mobile team on a visit.2. Settlements Without Family Doctors&#x2022;PAL-UA will deploy a family doctor to provide primary care, diagnostics, and referrals to specialists.&#x2022;Once 20 patients are registered for a specialist visit, they will travel with the mobile team to the settlement.3. Expansion of MHPSS services4. Home Visits for vulnerable groups</narrative>
  </description>
